{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery","id":1391515,"title":"Autochthonians and Sorcery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Alchemical Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-25T11:08:12-07:00","id":1391515,"title":"Autochthonians and Sorcery","content":"In previous Editions, sorcery only allowed for spells. Now it allows for sorcerous workings.<br /> <br /> Should Alchemicals be capable of sorcerous workings? Should Autochthonian mortals?<br /> <br /> Should sorcery somehow be impossible in Autochthonia?<br /> <br /> Should having your soul contained within a soulgem prevent one from being a sorceror?<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Celestial Compass: Autochthonia</i> was well-loved for introducing so much color and variety to the Realm of Brass and Shadows.<br /> <br /> Common humanity was joined by six elementally-mutated subspecies that took on the roles of barbarians, dwarves, elves, and goblins. None of them have soulgems, so if sorcery is possible in Autochthonia but impossible for those with soulgems, that would be a cool way to make the mutants even more weird and terrifying to the people of the Eight Nations.<br /> <br /> One of the Eight Nations had an immortality-chasing cult of thaumaturges that unwittingly killed themselves and used their soulgems to possess their own corpses like techno-liches. Which could still be done with a very specific thaumaturgical miracle instead of a &quot;procedure&quot;, but which could also be treated as a sorcerous working or even a Terrestrial Circle Spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T11:17:19-07:00","id":1391516,"title":"","content":"I find no reason about why they shouldnt.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals had their own bizarre sorcery.<br /> <br /> Why shouldn't them have their own sorcerous workings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T11:29:03-07:00","id":1391518,"title":"","content":"I think it's been suggested that in 3e alchemical protocols will just be straight up sorcery. The alchemicals and autochthonians have their own techy initiations and they call it something different but it's literally the same thing.<br /> <br /> Demon summoning won't work, unless the seal is breached, but elementals should be fair game. And Workings sound fine. That strikes me as the obvious way to do stuff like artifical limbs and various infrastructure not covered by alchemical charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T11:32:47-07:00","id":1391519,"title":"","content":"I would be very surprised if Pattern Weaving came back as a separate thing from sorcery in 3E. <br /> <br /> That might be what they call sorcery in Autochthonia. Similar to how the three circles are known as terrestrial, celestial, and solar or emerald, sapphire, and adamant depending on who you're talking to in creation. Maybe in Autochthonia the first two circles will be called man-machine weaving, and god-machine weaving. Perhaps titan-machine weaving for workings of the solar circle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T12:24:59-07:00","id":1391525,"title":"","content":"You know, I'm a tad conflicted. I can see the value of reducing cruft, but I also feel as though sorcery isn't quite an aesthetic fit for the Alchemical Exalted, even if one adds in some flavoured initiations; it still has the spells and the prospect of already published shaping rituals, and I can't help but find it out of sorts.<br /> <br /> If Pattern Weaving was to still be there, I'd imagine an equivalent to workings based on harnessing the infrastructure of Authochthon.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, soulgems only contain souls after a person has died (or if that procedure is used to violently remove their soul while still living). The gem in a forehead of a person isn't doing anything, it's there as a safety catch for when they would otherwise give up the ghost.<br /> <br /> I can only assume this was misunderstood by the writer who depicted Authochthonians as believing that Creation-born had no souls because they lacked gems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T14:55:43-07:00","id":1391558,"title":"","content":"I figure that mechanically, Alchemicals will have Sorcery.<br /> <br /> They'll probably have different Initiations that play up the whole &quot;I am an administrator of the Pattern Weave&quot; or whatever.<br /> <br /> I can see Workings being used to cleanse Blight Zones, but since those might be Adamant Workings I can see why they're not COMMON.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T16:24:20-07:00","id":1391565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1391525#post1391525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also feel as though sorcery isn't quite an aesthetic fit for the Alchemical Exalted, even if one adds in some flavoured initiations; it still has the spells and the prospect of already published shaping rituals, and I can't help but find it out of sorts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my issue.<br /> <br /> Alchemical Exalted have been defined by the limitations of how many physical Charms they can equip at one time. They can't even begin to perform sorcery or supernatural martial arts without installing the correct Charms for it.<br /> <br /> Sorcerous workings could provide an avenue for self-improvement outside of their Charms.<br /> <br /> Although, enchanting parts of your body as an Alchemical is a trickier thing than for other, non-Liminal Exalted. Alchemical Exalted are flayed to the bone in the Vats and have whole organs, systems, and limbs replaced simply to &quot;heal wounds&quot; or replace Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Pattern Weaving was to still be there, I'd imagine an equivalent to workings based on harnessing the infrastructure of Authochthon. </div> </div> </div>Which raises questions about how it would work <i>outside</i> of Autochthonia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T17:13:16-07:00","id":1391569,"title":"","content":"I think Weaving is confirmed as being a Sorcery Initiation (or multiple Sorcery Initiations). Beyond that, I\u2019m sure there are spells that don\u2019t exist in Autochthonia and ones that exist only there at the moment, but obviously that will change when the Seal is breached.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T10:07:54-07:00","id":1391702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1391558#post1391558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see Workings being used to cleanse Blight Zones, but since those might be Adamant Workings I can see why they're not COMMON.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still gives them more hope than they had before.<br /> <br /> But it also potentially gives them a way to cure Gremlin Syndrome. As well as giving Apostates another way to inflict it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T10:35:14-07:00","id":1391712,"title":"","content":"Actually, don't you think that in this case leaving Necromancy as a completely separate thing is somewhat arbitrary? <br /> <br /> I wonder whether Sorcerous Initiations isn't a bit of a missed opportunity to provide a uniform basis for genuinly different kinds of magic. (Say, we could introduce some system of keywords and make the choice of spells depend on your initiations).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T11:23:38-07:00","id":1391725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1391712#post1391712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, don't you think that in this case leaving Necromancy as a completely separate thing is somewhat arbitrary? <br /> <br /> I wonder whether Sorcerous Initiations isn't a bit of a missed opportunity to provide a uniform basis for genuinly different kinds of magic. (Say, we could introduce some system of keywords and make the choice of spells depend on your initiations).</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand necromancy is basically identical to sorcery but had no access to healing or nutrition stuff before presumably having access to something else that you can't do with sorcery. <br /> <br /> If weaving ends up being a separate system, this is what it would likely be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T11:28:38-07:00","id":1391729,"title":"","content":"AFAIK sorcery can't really affect the underworld much. That's necromancy's domain. There's probably other stuff too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T13:20:51-07:00","id":1391765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1391712#post1391712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, don't you think that in this case leaving Necromancy as a completely separate thing is somewhat arbitrary?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, many of us have suggested that, and we were surprised to learn that the developers are trying to make Necromancy its own separate thing.<br /> <br /> But we're willing to wait and see if they can deliver.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wonder whether Sorcerous Initiations isn't a bit of a missed opportunity to provide a uniform basis for genuinly different kinds of magic. (Say, we could introduce some system of keywords and make the choice of spells depend on your initiations). </div> </div> </div>No, I would rather all Sorcery be Sorcery and all Spells be Spells.<br /> <br /> Even for the Raksha.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1391725#post1391725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I understand necromancy is basically identical to sorcery but had no access to healing or nutrition stuff before presumably having access to something else that you can't do with sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>That distinction might matter if Sorcery had even one spell for healing comparable to its many, many, MANY spells for killing or cursing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T00:29:58-07:00","id":1391878,"title":"","content":"Necromancy kind of works still since it has some niceties in giving diversity to diffrent Exalts. It says something that Lunars can equal Solars at it in 3e, and the way that it is interacted with byt he different fomrs fo Creation's Exalts based on some hints by the devs I think is interesting.<br /> <br /> Weaving had a problem in that it was pretty much 100% used exclusively by one Exalt type, with this kind of attempt to be 1.5 and 2.5 sorcery when no one thought that was needed, there wasn't enough granulairyt for it, and it assumed I think to some extent ways the world worked that were not really the case until Weaving itself came about. It kind of feels weirdly just both hodgepodge (some astrology, some sorcery, some necromancy), and if anything just feels like an exotic subsystem to give Alchemcials More Unique Stuff than anything really solidly figured out. Especially when it was in itself a retcon of earlier stuff on them just using sorcery and that the Charms could easily have just been Man-Machine does emerald magic and God-Machien does sapphire magic and going from there.<br /> <br /> And again, since it was exclusive to Alchemicals (and Eclipse-alikes and Jadeborn I guess, neither of which is for sure in 3e), often just kind of had weird subsystems just for them, and often just reskinned sorcery and necromancy anyhow, I think it has a lot less idenity/leg to stand on than encromancy does. Something which has something to build on like Dragons of a Different Color and Smiling Rat are interesting. Some special magic that is basically reskinned sorcery-astrology-but-not that only is used by one Exalt type not seen in most games in teh default setting is a bit harder as ell I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T01:19:47-07:00","id":1391883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1391702#post1391702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still gives them more hope than they had before.<br /> <br /> But it also potentially gives them a way to cure Gremlin Syndrome. As well as giving Apostates another way to inflict it.</div> </div> </div> </div>unless, like the Great Curse, Gremlin Syndrome is stated as being outside the ability of Sorcery to cure. I don\u2019t know why you\u2019d assume Sorcery would necessarily be a solution here just because it\u2019s present. Similarly I can see Workings combating Blight Zones, but they\u2019re malignant growing things that are going to push back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T02:44:18-07:00","id":1391885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1391729#post1391729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIK sorcery can't really affect the underworld much. That's necromancy's domain. There's probably other stuff too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't summon and bind demons or elementals, which is a big thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T06:11:36-07:00","id":1391908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1391885#post1391885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can't summon and bind demons or elementals, which is a big thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Necromancy could really do with more impressive ghosts and other inhabitants of the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T06:40:24-07:00","id":1391910,"title":"","content":"I can see your point.<br /> <br /> I will say though that I think it's already somewhat improved over 2nd edition, because of this spell:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adversaries of the Righteous</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Summon the Shadow-Eaten (Ritual, 2wp; Instant):<br /> Summon an Essence 1-3 mortwight (Exalted, p.<br /> 505) or other monstrous ghost in a night-long ritual,<br /> rolling (Intelligence + Occult) against its Resolve to<br /> bind it for a year and a night. If this fails, roll (Wits +<br /> Occult) against its Willpower to banish it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2nd ed, IIRC, with Iron Circle, you could either summon ordinary ghosts (which I would argue is a very useful and flexible power, though in quite a different way to Summon Demon or Summon Elemental; it's an excellent information-gathering power, for example, and ghosts are generally a bit easier to control than demons), or screw it up and be attacked by spectres.<br /> You couldn't really go &quot;I want to summon up a combat-spirit to fight for me&quot; the way you can do with Summon Demon, unless you actually know, say, the name of a dead great warrior who died and became a ghost and learned some combat powers.<br /> <br /> But this spell lets you do this, summoning a mortwright, doppleganger, hungry ghost, rantai, susurrus, etc (maybe ghostfisher? Not sure if you could summon one with this spell). (As an aside, I think the ghosts in HDNP are some of the more solid entries, though I don't know how people have found them in practice, I haven't actually used any of them.)<br /> <br /> And I assume the standard Summon Ghost still exists as well, so you can summon up a murder victim to interrogate, your dead mum because you're sad, a ghost to spy for you who's more reliable than a demon, a dead PC so you can stuff him in his own animated corpse and then go on a crusade to free his people and then establish him as their ghost-king, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Also, one thing that necromancy is better at summoning than demons is armies. Summoning an army of demons is a giant hassle; you can only summon one per night, and you've got to keep an eye on them while you're building your army, lest they wander off and get into trouble (except Baidaks maybe. Baidaks are probably the best choice for a demon army).<br /> <br /> But with this spell:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adversaries of the Righteous</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raise the Rotting Horde (Control) (15sm, 1wp;<br /> Indefinite): Animate corpses as zombies, up to a size<br /> 2 battle group with poor Drill and Might 1. Zombies<br /> remain animated indefinitely unless exposed to sunlight<br /> for a full scene. As a control effect, the battle<br /> group has average Drill instead, or elite Drill by<br /> spending a Willpower while casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need a bunch of corpses of course, but this lets you summon up a battle group instantly. It'll only last a scene in daytime, but it'll last a whole night, and there are ways to keep them alive. The only way to get a battle group that fast with sorcery is having the second-circle demon games-box (I always forget her name, begins with S).<br /> <br /> Void Circle necromancy did have a spell to summon a Hekatonkhire, but it was quite generic compared to third-circle demons. Obviously, currently there are no rules for Third-Circle Demons anyway, but there will be, and there's plenty of fluff to get you started, whereas there's not for Hekatonkhires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T07:02:04-07:00","id":1391918,"title":"","content":"Summon big thing on par with third circle demon seems a pretty fair void circle effect.<br /> <br /> Just need to make sure to provide some good examples in the abyssal book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T07:42:08-07:00","id":1391930,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's the thing. Summon Hekatonkhire (ghost-thing of a third-circle daeva or behemoth) was a spell, but without all the cool descriptions of Malfeas's third circle menagerie, it fell a bit flat. Just a giant gribbly monster, rather than an Angel of Death, Avatar of the Apocalypse, all-consuming intelligent plague, black sun that blots out life, etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T07:57:10-07:00","id":1391937,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s a Hekatonkhire? I know that name from Wr20, but idr exactly what it is.<br /> <br /> Sorry. I don\u2019t know Exalted that well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T08:13:05-07:00","id":1391945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1391937#post1391937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s a Hekatonkhire? I know that name from Wr20, but idr exactly what it is.<br /> <br /> Sorry. I don\u2019t know Exalted that well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the undead equivalent to a behemoth; the ghost of a titan's flesh, the spiritual remnant of a dead Primordial's fetich, or a nightmare dreamt into existence by one of the Neverborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T10:09:37-07:00","id":1391985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1391883#post1391883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless, like the Great Curse, Gremlin Syndrome is stated as being outside the ability of Sorcery to cure. I don\u2019t know why you\u2019d assume Sorcery would necessarily be a solution here just because it\u2019s present.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you mean by &quot;cure&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean &quot;reverts your Dissonance back into Clarity&quot;. I don't meant &quot;eliminating any potential for relapse&quot; or &quot;eliminating any potential for contracting the disease&quot; or even &quot;inoculating against the disease&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T11:05:37-07:00","id":1391998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1391910#post1391910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(except Baidaks maybe. Baidaks are probably the best choice for a demon army)</div> </div> </div> </div>As the one who came up with the baidak originally, I've come to the conclusion that they were probably a mistake. In Sigereth's entry in the core, they're presented as constructs rather than demons; I expect that will remain the case, and they won't be summonable via Demon of the First Circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T12:01:25-07:00","id":1392012,"title":"","content":"Out of interest, why do you think they're a mistake? Is it because they're too undemonic (they don't have any wackiness or alienness to them), or for a different reason?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T14:36:44-07:00","id":1392050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1392012#post1392012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of interest, why do you think they're a mistake? Is it because they're too undemonic (they don't have any wackiness or alienness to them), or for a different reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>A core element of demon summoning in Exalted is that every demon's alien nature always offers potential complications; it isn't a Faustian bargain where they're trying to twist your intent, but you do need to work around their personalities and idiosyncrasies. Baidak don't have personalities and idiosyncrasies. The fact that so many discussions of what demons to summon eventually turns to &quot;you should summon baidak because they do exactly what they're told&quot; is a clear indication that they do indeed short-circuit this thematic element, and I consider this detrimental to the sorcerer play experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T14:41:50-07:00","id":1392052,"title":"","content":"I just figured that making them regular demons weakened the distinction of Sigereth's playbook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T14:49:57-07:00","id":1392056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1392050#post1392050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A core element of demon summoning in Exalted is that every demon's alien nature always offers potential complications; it isn't a Faustian bargain where they're trying to twist your intent, but you do need to work around their personalities and idiosyncrasies. Baidak don't have personalities and idiosyncrasies. The fact that so many discussions of what demons to summon eventually turns to &quot;you should summon baidak because they do exactly what they're told&quot; is a clear indication that they do indeed short-circuit this thematic element, and I consider this detrimental to the sorcerer play experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that seems pretty fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T14:52:53-07:00","id":1392058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1391985#post1391985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on what you mean by &amp;quot;cure&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean &amp;quot;reverts your Dissonance back into Clarity&amp;quot;. I don't meant &amp;quot;eliminating any potential for relapse&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;eliminating any potential for contracting the disease&amp;quot; or even &amp;quot;inoculating against the disease&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a massive number of assumptions built into this post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T15:24:57-07:00","id":1392064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1392058#post1392058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a massive number of assumptions built into this post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as?<br /> <br /> [ten char]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T18:53:59-07:00","id":1392092,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> thanks \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T19:40:19-07:00","id":1392107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery#post1391515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In previous Editions, sorcery only allowed for spells. Now it allows for sorcerous workings.<br /> <br /> Should Alchemicals be capable of sorcerous workings? Should Autochthonian mortals?<br /> <br /> Should sorcery somehow be impossible in Autochthonia?<br /> <br /> Should having your soul contained within a soulgem prevent one from being a sorceror?<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Celestial Compass: Autochthonia</i> was well-loved for introducing so much color and variety to the Realm of Brass and Shadows.<br /> <br /> Common humanity was joined by six elementally-mutated subspecies that took on the roles of barbarians, dwarves, elves, and goblins. None of them have soulgems, so if sorcery is possible in Autochthonia but impossible for those with soulgems, that would be a cool way to make the mutants even more weird and terrifying to the people of the Eight Nations.<br /> <br /> One of the Eight Nations had an immortality-chasing cult of thaumaturges that unwittingly killed themselves and used their soulgems to possess their own corpses like techno-liches. Which could still be done with a very specific thaumaturgical miracle instead of a &quot;procedure&quot;, but which could also be treated as a sorcerous working or even a Terrestrial Circle Spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>alchemicals had their own version of sorcery called protocols so I would assume they would get their own version of sorcerous workings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T23:14:51-07:00","id":1392131,"title":"","content":"Kind of to expand on my &quot;Weaving is only for Alchemicals and therefore kind of mostly useless&quot;, this is especially true in terms of support. We're gonna continue to get spells, example workings, artifacts, and stuff as the line evolves. Necromancy will get similar support in both the Abyssals and Liminals books, plus other books it might be handy. By being more shared systems, they're guranteed more support over the lifetime of th eline and not a lot needs to be done of rthat.<br /> <br /> Weaving short-circuits this for Alchemcials a bit. Because it's not sorcery, there's a lot that just doesn't flat-out work save what's called out as a cross-over (half-negating the point fo the sepration). Because they're to Autochthonia most of the time, it won't have nay real support out of that context. You will likely see nothing about it before an Alchemical book with Weaving, and similarly nothing afterwards save maybe the companion. And due to how it has been positioned to &quot;fill in&quot; for both sorcery and necromancy before, it means that Alchemicals usually got neither before, and there was an expectation to &quot;fill-in&quot; for them. It was something that how it was designed closed Alchemcials off to the generally more line-wide supported sorcery, and forced them to be using their onw special system that was often undersupported, needlessly complicated, and often diluted having ot use sorcery and necromancy <i>anyways</i> in order to fill in for these issues.<br /> <br /> Like, a big strength in the end is that it's something that's cool that if we asumed Weaving could get al lthe wordcount it needed. But often it eats up the section that'd of been sorcery in a book, but having to introduce its own mechanics and differences while at it. Kind of imagine if every sorcery-enhancing Charm, initation, bonus Merits, and spells were lumped together in one block fo text. Now think about how much you just stragiht-up <i>lose</i> having to explain Weaving. And also consider that it does not heavy-lifting for future wroks save teh Companion for that book.<br /> <br /> Like, Abyssals has to worry about this with necrmancy for instnace, sure. But it'll get more necromancy in Limnals. ANd who knows, <i>Paths of Brigid</i> or <i>Towers of the Mighty</i> might have some more that slides in there nicely. The Abyssal stuff will be load-bearing for future wroks. Weaving, by contrast, likely never gets that<br /> <br /> IN all this I just don't see a place for it. Especially since sorcery just kind of works anywhere: It's not about Creation's rules but reality in general. Autochthonia is just a different subset of Everything, even if a very isolated part of Evertyhing, and I think the idea that some Charms that Alchemicals can have installed let htem literally reality-hack, no matter hwere theya re, is fitting for sorcery just fine. ANd that they don't need extra 0.5 Circles to be cool with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T04:34:53-07:00","id":1392170,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's what it comes down to really. A third &quot;sorcery&quot; system, introduced in one of the last books in the run, with limited distinction from sorcery aside from aesthetics?<br /> <br /> People are just gonna re-skin sorcery to fill in the gaps. So you might as well just <i>make it sorcery</i>. Add some alchemical specific spells and a notes about what spells are known in autochthonia and you're good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T06:46:42-07:00","id":1392182,"title":"","content":"While I don't love that, as it was cool and fit them better as it's own thing, I can definitely see your point, Blaque and Elfive.<br /> <br /> And, as the first exposure we'll get to Alchemicals for years is in Essence, where stuff is going to be merged together for simplicity, I certainly think it's very likely that they'll just give them sorcery-slightly-changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T08:48:25-07:00","id":1392211,"title":"","content":"You can probably build a lot into the Weaving Module itself to help make the Alchemical experience different from other exalts.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T09:17:45-07:00","id":1392216,"title":"","content":"I forget, can mortals be necromancers?<br /> <br /> Should necromancy be possible in Autocthonia? If yes, imagine Apostate Alchemicals accessing necromancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T09:29:52-07:00","id":1392220,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a> I would say that necromancy would not be possible in Autochthonis because it doesn\u2019t really touch on the Underworld the way Creation does. But I\u2019m willing to listen to a counter-argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T09:32:16-07:00","id":1392221,"title":"","content":"They can, but a mortal necromancer can't also be a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Necromancy in Autocthonia... well, there's no Underworld or Shadowlands, and IIRC there are ghosts but not many. So I can't see a great deal of use out of it. It does seem kind of thematic for Voidbringers; it's not quite the same as the way their magic works, but in terms of corrupting Autocthon's spiritual landscape, it sort of makes sense.<br /> <br /> It seems fairly straightforward to just have them use a different initiation to the normal ones that focus on Shadowlands, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T09:39:34-07:00","id":1392222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1392216#post1392216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget, can mortals be necromancers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so.<br /> They gained the ability to learn Shadowlands Circle Necromancy in Scroll of Heroes so it's still possible for them to roll it back, however - it's unlikely they'll repeat the traits of Necromancy that made it so overpowered in mortal and Dragon-Blooded hands. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T09:43:21-07:00","id":1392225,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> sorcery and necromancy are mutually exclusive at higher levels, right? Like the same caster can\u2019t have four or five dots in both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T09:50:46-07:00","id":1392228,"title":"","content":"Not precisely.<br /> <br /> Solars can have up to level 3 sorcery and level 2 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Infernals can have up to level 3 sorcery and level 2 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Abyssals can have up to level 2 sorcery and level 3 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Lunars can have up to level 2 sorcery and level 2 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Sidereals can have up to level 2 sorcery and level 1 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Dragonblood can have up to level 1 sorcery. In 2nd edition certain DBs could instead have level 1 necromancy, but not both. I'm not sure what'll happen with that in 3rd edition (the full necromancy rules aren't out yet, after all).<br /> A very small number of mortals (and god-bloods, etc) can learn level 1 sorcery. In 2nd edition, it was possible for them to get level 1 necromancy, but not both. I assume that'll be the same in 3rd edition, but we'll see.<br /> <br /> Liminals, Getimians and Alchemicals we don't know about yet. Presumably Liminals are better at necromancy than sorcery, and Getimians better at sorcery than necromancy, but we'll see. In previous editions Alchemicals had a completely different set of Sorcery-esque powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-28-2020, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T09:54:23-07:00","id":1392231,"title":"","content":"Previously, Abyssals traded their ability to reach the Solar Circle of Sorcery for Void Circle Necromancy and Neph (who originally wrote Necromancy) on more than one occasion stated his intent was that no being should be able to access both. I guess we'll see if it holds?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T10:56:40-07:00","id":1392251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1392228#post1392228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not precisely.<br /> <br /> Solars can have up to level 3 sorcery and level 2 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Infernals can have up to level 3 sorcery and level 2 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Abyssals can have up to level 2 sorcery and level 3 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Lunars can have up to level 2 sorcery and level 2 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Sidereals can have up to level 2 sorcery and level 1 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Dragonblood can have up to level 1 sorcery. In 2nd edition certain DBs could instead have level 1 necromancy, but not both. I'm not sure what'll happen with that in 3rd edition (the full necromancy rules aren't out yet, after all).<br /> A very small number of mortals (and god-bloods, etc) can learn level 1 sorcery. In 2nd edition, it was possible for them to get level 1 necromancy, but not both. I assume that'll be the same in 3rd edition, but we'll see.<br /> <br /> Liminals, Getimians and Alchemicals we don't know about yet. Presumably Liminals are better at necromancy than sorcery, and Getimians better at sorcery than necromancy, but we'll see. In previous editions Alchemicals had a completely different set of Sorcery-esque powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's been explicitly stated yet whether a single 3e character can have both sorcery and necromancy? I'm guessing that you can only take one or the other for flavor and mechanical reasons, but I haven't discussed it with Vance yet. But if it is possible for Exalted to take both, I don't see Dragon-Blooded as being uniquely barred from doing the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T11:01:57-07:00","id":1392256,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1120_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1120\" data-vbnamecard=\"1120\">Eric Minton</a> thanks. That really clarifies things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T11:03:38-07:00","id":1392257,"title":"","content":"I think making it so solars have to choose between necromancy and sorcery will just ensure no solar ever takes necromancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T18:28:31-07:00","id":1392374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1392220#post1392220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a> I would say that necromancy would not be possible in Autochthonis because it doesn\u2019t really touch on the Underworld the way Creation does. But I\u2019m willing to listen to a counter-argument.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1392221#post1392221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Necromancy in Autocthonia... well, there's no Underworld or Shadowlands, and IIRC there are ghosts but not many. So I can't see a great deal of use out of it. It does seem kind of thematic for Voidbringers; it's not quite the same as the way their magic works, but in terms of corrupting Autocthon's spiritual landscape, it sort of makes sense.<br /> <br /> It seems fairly straightforward to just have them use a different initiation to the normal ones that focus on Shadowlands, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Autochthonia has Blight Zones, which were basically Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Autochthon has a massive chamber for storing the Higher Souls of people between incarnations.<br /> <br /> Necromancy doesn't deal only with souls, but also with corpses. For that matter, a Necromantic spell might be able to rip a soul out of a soulgem, as well as summon a ghost from Autochthon's ghost-chamber.<br /> <br /> If Necromancy can shape the substance of a Shadowland, a Blight Zone could also be a valid target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T18:39:31-07:00","id":1392377,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. Good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T01:39:50-07:00","id":1392447,"title":"","content":"It would make sense, if Weaving was simply a form of sorcery, for apostates to be able to get necromancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T08:47:21-07:00","id":1392552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1392447#post1392447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would make sense, if Weaving was simply a form of sorcery, for apostates to be able to get necromancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going farther, it would make sense if ONLY Apostates could get Necromancy. It would seem totally Unorthodox for Champions.<br /> <br /> I would not go so far as to suggest that Apostates would lose access to Sorcery. Being unable to cast spells their nation knows they know would be too obvious a tell that they had fallen, and would also remove some teeth from their threat level.<br /> <br /> Mortals should be able to learn Necromancy like in Creation. It's just in Autochthonia, doing so would practically always invoke the death penalty, and disqualify the soul from ever being considered for Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-29-2020, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T06:40:21-07:00","id":1394766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1392228#post1392228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not precisely.<br /> <br /> Solars can have up to level 3 sorcery and level 2 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Infernals can have up to level 3 sorcery and level 2 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Abyssals can have up to level 2 sorcery and level 3 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Lunars can have up to level 2 sorcery and level 2 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Sidereals can have up to level 2 sorcery and level 1 necromancy. Doesn't make a difference if you've got both.<br /> Dragonblood can have up to level 1 sorcery. In 2nd edition certain DBs could instead have level 1 necromancy, but not both. I'm not sure what'll happen with that in 3rd edition (the full necromancy rules aren't out yet, after all).<br /> A very small number of mortals (and god-bloods, etc) can learn level 1 sorcery. In 2nd edition, it was possible for them to get level 1 necromancy, but not both. I assume that'll be the same in 3rd edition, but we'll see.<br /> <br /> Liminals, Getimians and Alchemicals we don't know about yet. Presumably Liminals are better at necromancy than sorcery, and Getimians better at sorcery than necromancy, but we'll see. In previous editions Alchemicals had a completely different set of Sorcery-esque powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All of the above access to sorcery and necromancy is absolutely correct under 2e rules, with the exception of the Lunars' access to necromancy, which was level 1, not 2, per the Black Treatise. However, it looks like Fangs at the Gate p. 310 says Lunars can be the equal of Solars in necromancy, so 3e may be changing things up.<br /> <br /> Also, in the 2e Alchemicals book it says that Alchemicals that have gone Gremlin and have a corrupted Man-Machine Protocol Weaving Engine CAN access regular sorcery and necromancy to the 1st level of each, and if they have a corrupted God-Machine Protocol Weaving Engine, then they get their choice of level 2 sorcery OR level 2 necromancy, but not both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T10:57:16-07:00","id":1395108,"title":"","content":"For me, the big difference isn't how magic works, it's the environment. You have elementals, but they are a different set. There are the deva subsouls, which presumably could be summoned if the higher up souls allow it. You cast magma krakens or summon rust monsters, what does that do to the Maker's body? You just punched a hole in some nutrient lines, or destroyed a sensor-nerve. That would probably get attention from white-blood-cell equivalent spirits, and maybe make the devas declare sanctions on your country, even if the body doesn't reflexivly spasm and squish you. Eyeless face, if it's even possible to summon them into the jouten's region of Elsewhere, would likely ping as Blight or gremlin. I could see the Weaving Protocol being designed to specifically lock out certain high-collateral-damage spells. Which is a restriction that could be lifted if the Alchemical was going into creation. Or, there are just spells that no one in there knows, so can't be taught.<br /> <br /> As for necromancy, the Blight and such seems more &quot;active&quot;, where Creations Underworld is &quot;neverborn dreaming as everything gets slowly sucked into the Abyss&quot;. So I would have necromancy as... less reliable? You'll get roughly what you want, but each spell will be twisted to better serve the Blight.<br /> <br /> The ultimate Working, of course, should be &quot;jump-starting the Great Maker's brain&quot;. Biggest. Lightning bolt. Evah. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1391565#post1391565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemical Exalted have been defined by the limitations of how many physical Charms they can equip at one time. They can't even begin to perform sorcery or supernatural martial arts without installing the correct Charms for it.<br /> <br /> Sorcerous workings could provide an avenue for self-improvement outside of their Charms.<br /> <br /> Although, enchanting parts of your body as an Alchemical is a trickier thing than for other, non-Liminal Exalted. Alchemical Exalted are flayed to the bone in the Vats and have whole organs, systems, and limbs replaced simply to &quot;heal wounds&quot; or replace Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why go to the trouble of a Working when Autochthon society is practically tailor-made for Artifact creation. Dunno, I can imagine the concept but at my table I would have to rule &quot;no Working can alter the Alchemical body&quot; because aesthetic. On the other hand, I would want them to be easily able to integrate artifacts into their body. Some sort of rules where Artifacts could be more powerful, but more specialized than charms. Maybe a way to trade charm slots for artifact slots, or maybe not.<br /> <br /> Weird idea. You can have an artifact arm, infernals had an artifact heart. The Alchemical &quot;self&quot; being just brain &amp; soulgem, imagine an Artifact head. And now I'm reminded of C-3P0. All those artifact body parts that keep getting shot off the chassis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T12:27:01-07:00","id":1395128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpoonR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1391515-autochthonians-and-sorcery?p=1395108#post1395108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the big difference isn't how magic works, it's the environment. You have elementals, but they are a different set. There are the deva subsouls, which presumably could be summoned if the higher up souls allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And which the subsouls could punish, if they deem the Champion's situation does not merit a summoning. Alternatively, if they deem the situation pressing, but not pressing enough for their personal visitation, they could respond to the summoning by sending servant-spirits to aid the Champion.<br /> <br /> After all, sending servants in response to a summoning is certainly an option the subsouls would want, since that's an effective way to punish frivolous summons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You cast magma krakens or summon rust monsters, what does that do to the Maker's body? You just punched a hole in some nutrient lines, or destroyed a sensor-nerve. That would probably get attention from white-blood-cell equivalent spirits, and maybe make the devas declare sanctions on your country, even if the body doesn't reflexivly spasm and squish you. Eyeless face, if it's even possible to summon them into the jouten's region of Elsewhere, would likely ping as Blight or gremlin. I could see the Weaving Protocol being designed to specifically lock out certain high-collateral-damage spells. Which is a restriction that could be lifted if the Alchemical was going into creation. Or, there are just spells that no one in there knows, so can't be taught. </div> </div> </div>Or only Alchemicals who are trusted to wield wide-scale destruction power are given access to information about such spells.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why go to the trouble of a Working when Autochthon society is practically tailor-made for Artifact creation. </div> </div> </div>Why spend as much for sorcery when you get less than half of what sorcery offers anyone else?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dunno, I can imagine the concept but at my table I would have to rule &quot;no Working can alter the Alchemical body&quot; because aesthetic. </div> </div> </div>The modularity of the Alchemical body might be sufficient deterrent on its own. Why enchant your eye when your eye is probably getting replaced entirely to install a new Charm?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand, I would want them to be easily able to integrate artifacts into their body. </div> </div> </div>They already had Charms for integrating artifacts into their body. One allowed them to fold up artifacts and store them in their bodies, to be retrieved for use later. Another allowed them to generate pre-loaded facsimile artifacts, like Glorious Solar Saber, presumably including potential for Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}